{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-52803","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100774","text":"Lane B — build studbook"}]},{"id":"blk-52804","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100775","marks":["bold"],"text":"Owns:"},{"id":"spn-100776","text":" "},{"id":"spn-100777","marks":["code"],"text":"studbook/"},{"id":"spn-100778","text":" "},{"id":"spn-100779","marks":["bold"],"text":"Must not touch:"},{"id":"spn-100780","text":" "},{"id":"spn-100781","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM/forge/"},{"id":"spn-100782","text":" (substrate — consume it, never reimplement it), "},{"id":"spn-100783","marks":["code"],"text":"RRABBIT/m2/"},{"id":"spn-100784","text":", root "},{"id":"spn-100785","marks":["code"],"text":"*.md"},{"id":"spn-100786","text":"."}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-52806","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100787","text":"## ❌ BLOCKED. Do not write schema until two things are ruled  1. "},{"id":"spn-100788","marks":["bold"],"text":"studbook §10.5 — does the identity ladder admit a new prefix?"},{"id":"spn-100789","text":" A studbook record is not a    "},{"id":"spn-100790","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-"},{"id":"spn-100791","text":", "},{"id":"spn-100792","marks":["code"],"text":"scen-"},{"id":"spn-100793","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-100794","marks":["code"],"text":"replay-"},{"id":"spn-100795","text":". If the answer is no, studbook is keyed by something else and the    schema changes shape. 2. "},{"id":"spn-100796","marks":["bold"],"text":"The index question"},{"id":"spn-100797","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-100798","marks":["code"],"text":"CONFIDENTIALITY.md"},{"id":"spn-100799","text":" §4) — accept, minimise, or encrypt the    operator-visible graph. This decides what columns exist.  Both are "},{"id":"spn-100800","marks":["bold"],"text":"[TRAVIS]"},{"id":"spn-100801","text":". Reading, and the prolly-tree finding below, can proceed meanwhile."}]}],"id":"blk-52805","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-52807","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100802","text":"Read first, in this order"}]},{"id":"blk-52808","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-52810","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100803","marks":["code"],"text":"studbook/docs/spec/README.md"},{"id":"spn-100804","text":" — the whole spec. Its header says *\"draft spec. No"}]}],"id":"blk-52809","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-52811","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100805","text":"implementation. Nothing in §7 or §10 has been ruled. Do not build from this yet.\"* That still holds for §7 and §10."}]},{"id":"blk-52812","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-52814","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100806","marks":["code"],"text":"PUBLISH_PATH.md"},{"id":"spn-100807","text":" — studbook's first named consumer."}]}],"id":"blk-52813","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-52816","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100808","marks":["code"],"text":"CONFIDENTIALITY.md"},{"id":"spn-100809","text":" — §4 is the tension that decides the schema."}]}],"id":"blk-52815","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-52818","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100810","marks":["code"],"text":"STACK_HUB.md"},{"id":"spn-100811","text":" §0.8 — why Postgres is right for the index and catastrophic for the bytes."}]}],"id":"blk-52817","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-52819","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100812","text":"What studbook is, in one line"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-52821","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100813","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"A record in studbook carries where it came from, and a record that cannot show its provenance is refused rather than stored.\""}]}],"id":"blk-52820","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-52822","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100814","text":"What is decided"}]},{"id":"blk-52823","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-52825","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100815","marks":["bold"],"text":"Supabase is abandoned"},{"id":"spn-100816","text":" (2026-07-30). studbook replaces it. "},{"id":"spn-100817","marks":["bold"],"text":"Nothing migrates"},{"id":"spn-100818","text":" until studbook"}]}],"id":"blk-52824","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-52826","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100819","text":"holds the same data with the same guarantees — "},{"id":"spn-100820","marks":["code"],"text":"fleet.*"},{"id":"spn-100821","text":" serves KILN and FleetPrompt "},{"id":"spn-100822","marks":["italic"],"text":"today"},{"id":"spn-100823","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-52827","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-52829","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100824","marks":["bold"],"text":"Postgres is the index, R2 holds the bytes."},{"id":"spn-100825","text":" Measured: bytes in Postgres is "},{"id":"spn-100826","marks":["bold"],"text":"18.7×"},{"id":"spn-100827","text":" R2 and"}]}],"id":"blk-52828","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-52830","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100828","text":"puts every tier underwater — a 10 TB customer would cost "},{"id":"spn-100829","marks":["bold"],"text":"$2,867/month"},{"id":"spn-100830","text":". The same customer's "},{"id":"spn-100831","marks":["italic"],"text":"index"},{"id":"spn-100832","text":" is ~250 MB, or "},{"id":"spn-100833","marks":["bold"],"text":"seven cents"},{"id":"spn-100834","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-52831","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-52833","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100835","marks":["bold"],"text":"This does not reverse §2."},{"id":"spn-100836","text":" §2 rejected Postgres as the "},{"id":"spn-100837","marks":["italic"],"text":"data model"},{"id":"spn-100838","text":" — a row does not say why it"}]}],"id":"blk-52832","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-52834","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100839","text":"is that row. As an "},{"id":"spn-100840","marks":["bold"],"text":"index over content-addressed blobs"},{"id":"spn-100841","text":", the refusal still comes from content addressing and Postgres only makes it queryable. "},{"id":"spn-100842","marks":["bold"],"text":"Never describe this as \"studbook moved back to Postgres.\""}]},{"id":"blk-52835","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-52837","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100843","marks":["bold"],"text":"Postgres lives on the Hetzner VM"},{"id":"spn-100844","text":" (lane C), managed by Pigsty, shared with nothing that has a"}]}],"id":"blk-52836","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-52838","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100845","text":"user's bytes in it."}]},{"id":"blk-52839","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-52841","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100846","marks":["bold"],"text":"Enterprise clients get their own VM and their own database."},{"id":"spn-100847","text":" Single-tenant, which sidesteps"}]}],"id":"blk-52840","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-52842","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100848","text":"§10.2 for them entirely."}]},{"id":"blk-52843","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100849","text":"Substrate you must consume rather than rebuild"}]},{"id":"blk-52844","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100850","text":"studbook §4: "},{"id":"spn-100851","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"If studbook reimplements something substrate already proves, that is a finding, not a shortcut.\""},{"id":"spn-100852","text":" "},{"id":"spn-100853","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM/forge/"},{"id":"spn-100854","text":" already ships, with batteries:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-52846","spans":[{"id":"spn-100855","text":"Capability"}]},{"id":"blk-52847","spans":[{"id":"spn-100856","text":"Where"}]},{"id":"blk-52848","spans":[{"id":"spn-100857","text":"Guarantee"}]}],"id":"blk-52845","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-52849","spans":[{"id":"spn-100858","text":"Content-addressed store"}]},{"id":"blk-52850","spans":[{"id":"spn-100859","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_store.py"},{"id":"spn-100860","text":" "},{"id"