h","spans":[{"id":"spn-100906","marks":["bold"],"text":"The parity gate"},{"id":"spn-100907","text":" before anything migrates: same reads, same refusals, side by side with"}]}],"id":"blk-52881","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-52883","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100908","text":"Supabase still up."}]},{"id":"blk-52884","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100909","text":"The prolly-tree finding — do this while blocked"}]},{"id":"blk-52885","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100910","text":"§7.3 proposes a prolly tree for §6.1's index gap and calls itself "},{"id":"spn-100911","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"a reading task before it is a build task.\""},{"id":"spn-100912","text":" But "},{"id":"spn-100913","marks":["code"],"text":"STACK_HUB.md"},{"id":"spn-100914","text":" §0.8 argues "},{"id":"spn-100915","marks":["bold"],"text":"Postgres may simply be the answer"},{"id":"spn-100916","text":" — ordered access and range scans today, at the cost of history-independence and cheap subtree diff."}]},{"id":"blk-52886","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100917","marks":["bold"],"text":"Produce a written finding on which trade is right."},{"id":"spn-100918","text":" That is a real deliverable and it needs no ruling. Do not start building a prolly tree."}]},{"id":"blk-52887","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100919","text":"Traps"}]},{"id":"blk-52888","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-52890","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100920","text":"**A track records a "},{"id":"spn-100921","marks":["italic"],"text":"live OS world"},{"id":"spn-100922","text":", not a sealed "},{"id":"spn-100923","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-"},{"id":"spn-100924","text":" world.** Conflating them is the plan's"}]}],"id":"blk-52889","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-52891","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100925","text":"R9 and it "},{"id":"spn-100926","marks":["bold"],"text":"fails quietly"},{"id":"spn-100927","text":" — WRLM's passing test counts would appear to back OS-world claims they do not touch."}]},{"id":"blk-52892","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-52894","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100928","marks":["bold"],"text":"Convergent encryption is refused by name."},{"id":"spn-100929","text":" Deriving the key from the plaintext restores"}]}],"id":"blk-52893","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-52895","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100930","text":"cross-user dedup and looks like free money; it also restores the confirmation-of-a-file attack §6.2 identified. Per-user dedup has none of this and is where the saving is."}]},{"id":"blk-52896","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-52898","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100931","marks":["bold"],"text":"studbook §9's non-goals are load-bearing."},{"id":"spn-100932","text":" Not a general database, not a SQLite competitor, not"}]}],"id":"blk-52897","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-52899","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100933","text":"a new identity rung without §10.5. A hub asking for joins is not a reason to relax them."}]},{"id":"blk-52900","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-52902","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100934","marks":["bold"],"text":"`studbook/` is a local-only git repo with no remote."},{"id":"spn-100935","text":" Commits survive; pushes have nowhere to"}]}],"id":"blk-52901","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-52903","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100936","text":"go. Do not assume it is backed up."}]},{"id":"blk-52904","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-52906","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100937","text":"Travis said on 2026-08-15 that studbook runs on Fly with a site at "},{"id":"spn-100938","marks":["code"],"text":"studbook.computedriven.com"},{"id":"spn-100939","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-52905","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-52907","kind":